1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
When Andy met Edie, life imitated art.

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Factory Girl is a drama, history film directed by George Hickenlooper.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
In the mid-1960s, wealthy debutant Edie Sedgwick meets artist Andy Warhol.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
She joins Warhol's famous Factory and becomes his muse.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Although she seems to have it all, Edie cannot have the love she craves from Andy, and she has an affair with
a charismatic musician, who pushes her to seek independence from the artist and the milieu.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Edie Sedgwick, played by Sienna Miller.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Andy Warhol, played by Guy Pearce.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Musician, played by Hayden Christensen.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Richie Berlin, played by Mena Suvari.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Chuck Wein, played by Jimmy Fallon.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Brigid Polk, played by Tara Summers.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Factory Girl is a 2006 American biographical film
directed by George Hickenlooper.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
It is based on the rapid rise and fall of 1960s underground film star and socialite Edie Sedgwick
(Sienna Miller), known for her association with the artist Andy Warhol (Guy Pearce).

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Factory Girl was released by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer (through MGM Distribution Co.) on December 29, 2006, to
largely negative reviews from critics, who nonetheless praised Miller's performance as Sedgwick.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The film grossed $3.6 million against a $7 million budget.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film explores themes of infidelity, new york city, gallery, alcohol, studio.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The tone is emotional.
